  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as both a noun and a suru verb. Applies to laws, regulations, tariffs, restrictions, and systems. Implies that the item in question is completely removed, not simply reformed or revised. Common in political, economic, and policy discussions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {規制|きせい}を{撤廃|てっぱい}する: to abolish regulations\n- {関税|かんぜい}の{撤廃|てっぱい}: abolition of tariffs\n- {制限|せいげん}を{撤廃|てっぱい}する: to remove restrictions\n- {制度|せいど}の{撤廃|てっぱい}: abolition of a system\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {廃止|はいし}: abolition, discontinuation (broader, includes services and practices)\n- {廃棄|はいき}: disposal, scrapping (physical objects or agreements)",
